1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,270
Welcome to the Articulate Journal.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,040
I'm Russell, and I've spent most of my

3
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,750
career designing and
building software systems.

4
00:00:07,830 --> 00:00:11,920
Over the years, I've learned
that architecture isn't

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,380
really about drawing diagrams

6
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,920
or choosing technologies.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,390
It's about making decisions

8
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:19,600
and understanding the consequences
of those decisions over time.

9
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,560
Today, we are at the beginning

10
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,750
of another major shift in our industry.

11
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:27,480
Artificial intelligence
isn't just changing

12
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:31,200
how we write software. It's changing
how we think about architecture itself.

13
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:35,580
We're seeing new ideas
emerge almost daily:

14
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:38,660
Agentic systems. AI-native applications.

15
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:42,970
Multi-agent architectures.
Durable execution.

16
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,600
Memory, reasoning and retrieval.

17
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:48,780
But while the tools are evolving rapidly,

18
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:50,960
one question keeps coming back to me.

19
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:53,440
How do we build AI-native systems

20
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:55,760
that are reliable, understandable

21
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:58,080
and maintainable in the real world?

22
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:00,960
That's the question behind Articulate.

23
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:02,560
Articulate isn't a demo

24
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,240
project or a proof of concept.

25
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:05,740
It's a real software platform

26
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:08,250
that I'm designing and building in public,

27
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:12,320
with the goal of exploring what
AI-native architecture looks like

28
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,450
when you approach it
as a systems architect.

29
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:18,060
More importantly, this
journal isn't a retrospective.

30
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,760
I'm not waiting until
everything is finished

31
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:22,970
before explaining how it all works.

32
00:01:23,050 --> 00:01:26,000
Instead, I'm documenting
the journey as it happens.

33
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:30,160
The ideas, research,
architectural decisions,

34
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:33,560
trade-offs and mistakes,
and sometimes discovering

35
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,210
the best decision is to change direction.

36
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:38,120
Because that's part of architecture:

37
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,350
a continuous process of learning,

38
00:01:40,430 --> 00:01:42,200
questioning and refining.

39
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,770
Throughout this journal, I'll explore

40
00:01:44,850 --> 00:01:47,430
the principles behind AI-native systems,

41
00:01:47,510 --> 00:01:50,050
investigate new architectural patterns,

42
00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:51,940
evaluate technologies against

43
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:53,610
real architectural requirements,

44
00:01:53,690 --> 00:01:55,360
and gradually build Articulate

45
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,700
into a working platform.

46
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:00,100
Some episodes will focus on concepts.

47
00:02:00,410 --> 00:02:02,800
Others will follow architectural decisions

48
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:06,570
from the original question
through to implementation.

49
00:02:06,650 --> 00:02:08,200
The software is important,

50
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,220
but the reasoning behind the software

51
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:12,690
is what I really want to preserve.

52
00:02:12,790 --> 00:02:15,680
If you're interested in
software architecture,

53
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:18,440
AI-native systems, or
simply want to follow

54
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:21,320
the design of a complex
system as it evolves,

55
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:24,010
then I hope you'll enjoy the journey.

56
00:02:24,090 --> 00:02:26,920
Welcome to the Articulate Journal.

